Website top cover illustration, wide 16:9.
Art style (required, always): 16-bit RPG style pixel art with clearly visible square pixels, limited palette, bold dark outline, 2–3 tone shading, small highlights; no smooth gradients, no painterly, vector, watercolor or 3D look.
Match the characters' proportions and colors of the attached reference images exactly, drawn in this same pixel-art style.
Bright daytime laboratory mood, soft natural sunlight through large windows, clean white walls, light lavender, mint and pink accents.
Scene: a sunny corner of the laboratory turned into an art studio, two wooden easels with canvases seen from the back, a low round posing platform, a wooden posable drawing mannequin, paint jars and brushes.
Characters:
  the Fruit Fly researcher (tiny cartoon fruit fly, large red compound eyes, retro dark blue helmet with a yellow-white stripe, colorful dangling cables, tiny white lab coat, translucent wings), on the left facing right, holding a thin brush at the left easel;
  AbaBot (boxy beige retro CRT-monitor robot, dark green screen face with mint pixel eyes, short antenna topped with a red-brown abacus bead, gray segmented arms, small tank treads), on the right facing left, holding a big brush at the right easel;
  Haru (lab assistant girl, long straight pink hair with navy streaks and a thick navy streak down the center of the bangs, two round hair buns on top, blue eyes, lavender hoodie, open white lab coat, rolled-up jeans, lavender sneakers) standing on the posing platform in the center, one hand on hip;
  Sia (maid intern, long straight jet-black hair, no headdress, gray eyes, charcoal-black long-sleeved maid dress, large gray bow at the collar, long white frilled apron) and Moa (maid intern, long ash-beige wavy hair, white frilled maid headband with a white ribbon over the left ear, amber eyes, camel knit cardigan, red and navy plaid bow tie, white frilled apron, black skirt) standing beside the platform waiting their turn;
  the Professor (chibi male scientist, dark charcoal spiky hair with a white streak at the front, very thick black eyebrows, teal rectangular glasses, white lab coat over a black vest and black tie) at the back center pointing at a blank whiteboard with simple circle-and-line shapes;
  three small cute dark navy silhouette judges with white dot eyes (one with a pink side-ponytail bow, one with a beret and teal-glinting round glasses, one with a cat-ear hood and yellow pompoms) sitting at a small judges' table in the back right holding blank score paddles.
Visual metaphor: the wooden drawing mannequin next to Haru takes exactly the same pose as her.
Composition: every face and hand inside the central safe area (12% margin left and right, 10% top, 18% bottom); bottom-left corner plain and bright; the light falls on the posing platform.
Mood: curious, friendly rivalry, the moment before the painting starts.
No text, no letters, no numbers, no logos, no weapons, no cigarettes, no alcohol, no blood, no real brands.

